{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Law of Formation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Law of Formation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"law of formation law of formation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Law of Formation.md","fileName":"Law of Formation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Law of Formation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Sequences and Algebraic Patterns]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Sequences and Algebraic Patterns","Sequence","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Law of Formation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Law of Formation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"law of formation law of formation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Law of Formation.md","fileName":"Law of Formation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Law of Formation","heading":"Law of Formation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A law of formation is a rule that generates the members of a pattern or [[Sequence]]. It can describe how to obtain each term from earlier terms or give a direct formula from the term's position.\n\nFor (2,7,12,17,\\ldots), the recursive law adds five each time, while the direct law gives the (n)th term as (2+5(n-1)). A proposed law should reproduce every listed case and specify which positions are allowed. Algebraic notation makes the rule reusable without enumerating the infinitely many terms it can generate.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Sequences and Algebraic Patterns","Sequence","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Law of Formation.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Law of Formation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"law of formation law of formation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Law of Formation.md","fileName":"Law of Formation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Law of Formation","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Sequences and Algebraic Patterns","Sequence","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}